              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#the_multiplicative_monoid_of_the_natural_numbers"} The multiplicative monoid of the natural numbers
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#other_examples"} Other examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Absorption monoids are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+objects"} monoid objects
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+sets"} pointed sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+objects"} monoid objects
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            An
            %strong absorption monoid
            or
            %strong annihilation monoid
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (M,1,\cdot)
            that is also an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absorption+magma"} absorption magma
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (M,0)
          %p
            Equivalently, it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+sets"} pointed sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdot
            by any element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            preserves the point
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#initial_and_terminal_absorption_monoids Initial and terminal absorption monoids
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
            absorption monoid is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝟚
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2}
            with elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝟚
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in \mathbb{2}
            representing
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/false"} false
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝟚
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \in \mathbb{2}
            representing
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝟚
                  %mo ×
                  %mi 𝟚
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝟚
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\cdot(-):\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{2} \to \mathbb{2}
            representing
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjunction"} conjunction
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
            absorption monoid is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+monoid"} trivial monoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝟙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strictly+terminal"} strictly terminal
          %h3#absorption_monoid_homomorphisms Absorption monoid homomorphisms
          %p
            Given absorption monoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:M \to N
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(0) = 0
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(1) = 1
            %li
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in M
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in M
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(a \cdot b) = h(a) \cdot h(b)
          %h3#ideals_and_antiideals Ideals and anti-ideals
          %p
            A two-sided
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            of an absorption monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is a subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in I
            %li
              for all elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in M
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in M
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \cdot b \in I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in I
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in I
          %p
            A two-sided anti-ideal of an absorption monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is a subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \notin I
            %li
              for all elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in M
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in I
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in I
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \cdot b \in I
          %h3#quotient_absorption_monoids Quotient absorption monoids
          %p
            Given an absorption monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            and a two-sided ideal
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
            absorption monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M/I
            with absorption monoid homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:M \to M/I
            such that for all elements
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in I
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i(a) = 0
          %h3#invertible_elements Invertible elements
          %p
            An element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in M
            is an
            %strong invertible element
            or a
            %strong unit
            if there exists an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in M
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \cdot b = 1
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \cdot a = 1
          %p
            The set of invertible elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^\times
            in an absorption monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is always closed under multiplication; i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^\times
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submonoid"} submonoid
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^\times
            forms a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
          %h3#division_monoids Division monoids
          %p
            An absorption monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+monoid"} division monoid
            if every non-invertible element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is equal to zero.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is Heyting if there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+apartness+relation"} tight apartness relation
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            such that every invertible element is apart from zero, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is discrete if every element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is either zero or invertible.
          %h3#regular_elements Regular elements
          %p
            An element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in M
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong regular element
            = succeed "," do
              %strong cancellative element
            %strong cancellable element
            if for all elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in M
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = c
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \cdot b = a \cdot c
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi c
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \cdot a = c \cdot b
          %p
            The set of regular elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Reg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Reg}(M)
            in an absorption monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is always closed under multiplication; i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Reg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Reg}(M)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submonoid"} submonoid
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %h3#integral_monoids Integral monoids
          %p
            An absorption monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+monoid"} integral monoid
            if every non-regular element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is equal to zero.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is Heyting if there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+apartness+relation"} tight apartness relation
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            such that every regular element is apart from zero, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is discrete if every element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is either zero or regular.
          %h3#ore_sets_and_ore_absorption_monoids Ore sets and Ore absorption monoids
          %p
            Given an absorption monoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ore+set"} Ore set
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submonoid"} submonoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Reg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Reg}(M)
            such that every element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            satisfies the left and right Ore conditions:
          %ul
            %li
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in M
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \cdot d = b \cdot c
            %li
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in M
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi c
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \cdot a = c \cdot b
          %p
            A absorption monoid is an Ore absorption monoid if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Reg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Reg}(M)
            is an Ore set.
          %h3#localization_and_group_completion Localization and group completion
          %p
            The localization of an Ore integral monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Reg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Reg}(M)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+monoid"} division monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+monoid"} localization
            of an absorption monoid at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            is the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+group"} trivial group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
            of any absorption monoid is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+group"} trivial group
          %h3#actions_and_modules Actions and modules
          %p
            Given an absorption monoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P, 0)
            is a binary function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi L
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo ×
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_L:M \times P \to P
            such that:
          %ul
            %li
              for all elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_L(1, p) = p
            %li
              for all elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in M
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in M
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_L(a, \alpha_L(b, c)) = \alpha_L(a \cdot b, c)
            %li
              for all elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_L(0, p) = 0
            %li
              for all elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_L(a, 0) = 0
          %p
            A right
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P, 0)
            is a binary function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo ×
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_R:P \times M \to P
            such that:
          %ul
            %li
              for all elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_R(p, 1) = p
            %li
              for all elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in M
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in M
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_R(\alpha_R(c, a), b) = \alpha_R(c, a \cdot b)
            %li
              for all elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_R(p, 0) = 0
            %li
              for all elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
